{
  "duration": 56.199,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.119,
      "end": 0.319,
      "text": "So"
    },
    {
      "start": 0.919,
      "end": 1.979,
      "text": "welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.419,
      "end": 3.839,
      "text": "Time for one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.4,
      "end": 8.159,
      "text": "Now in this problem, a train travels at fifty kilometer per hour"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.619,
      "end": 10.599,
      "text": "and reaches the station in four hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.199,
      "end": 12.359,
      "text": "The question is asking us"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.819,
      "end": 17.639,
      "text": "how much extra time the train would take if its speed were only forty kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.119,
      "end": 18.42,
      "text": "First,"
    },
    {
      "start": 18.879,
      "end": 20.239,
      "text": "let us find the total distance."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.719,
      "end": 22.079,
      "text": "Distance is equal to speed"
    },
    {
      "start": 22.539,
      "end": 23.439,
      "text": "multiplied by time."
    },
    {
      "start": 23.859,
      "end": 25.399,
      "text": "So distance is equal to fifty"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.819,
      "end": 26.819,
      "text": "multiplied by four,"
    },
    {
      "start": 27.34,
      "end": 29.019,
      "text": "which gives us two hundred kilometer."
    },
    {
      "start": 29.479,
      "end": 31.679,
      "text": "Now we know the distance, so we can find the new time."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.159,
      "end": 34.399,
      "text": "Time is equal to distance divided by speed."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.979,
      "end": 38.36,
      "text": "So the new time is two hundred divided by forty, which is five hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.899,
      "end": 39.739,
      "text": "But be careful here."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.139,
      "end": 42.5,
      "text": "The question is not asking for the new total time."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.979,
      "end": 51.459,
      "text": "It is asking how much longer the journey would take. So extra time is equal to five hours minus four hours, which is one hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.919,
      "end": 52.279,
      "text": "Hence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 52.659,
      "end": 56.199,
      "text": "the final answer is one hour, which is option B."
    }
  ],
